  "reason": "The current best is config_039 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.7250. Evidence strongly supports scvi_n200 as the best RNA encoder, multiprofile as essential, weighted fusion over concat (+0.025), and imagenet_vit_l over resnet50 (+0.012). The only untested minor variant of this top configuration is swapping transformer aggregation for avgpool while keeping weighted fusion. In RNA-only, transformer vs avgpool made negligible difference (0.6530 vs 0.6501), but in the multimodal setting with a strong image encoder the interaction could differ slightly. Since this is the final experiment, config_037 is the safest exploitation of the current best: it preserves all top-performing components (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, weighted fusion) and only tests the one remaining untested aggregation variant, giving the best chance of matching or marginally exceeding 0.7250 without risking a large drop from switching to concat fusion."
